# shadcn/ui Components

This project uses [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com) for all UI elements. The configuration lives in [components.json](mdc:components.json), and installed components are placed in [components/ui](mdc:components/ui).

## Rules

- Always prefer shadcn/ui components over building UI primitives from scratch.
- Do not hand-write components that already exist in the shadcn registry (e.g. `button`, `input`, `dialog`, `card`, etc.) — install them instead.
- Use the aliases defined in [components.json](mdc:components.json):
  - UI components: `@/components/ui`
  - Utilities: `@/lib/utils`
  - Hooks: `@/hooks`

## Initializing shadcn/ui

If shadcn/ui has not yet been initialized in the project (i.e. `components.json` is missing), run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding components

Whenever a shadcn component is needed but not yet installed under [components/ui](mdc:components/ui), install it via the CLI before importing it. For example, to add the `button` component:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

Replace `button` with the name of the component you need (e.g. `dialog`, `card`, `dropdown-menu`). Multiple components can be added in a single command:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button card dialog
```

After installation, import the component from `@/components/ui/<component-name>`.
